## Why This Is Asked
Auditing and non-repudiation in CNF gateways are critical for multi-tenant environments. This question validates practical expertise with Kubernetes Secrets, HMAC signing, sidecar log pipelines, and retention configuration—essential skills for implementing post-deployment security controls.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped auditing and non-repudiation
- HMAC signing using per-tenant Kubernetes Secrets
- Sidecar-based log forwarding to in-cluster sinks
- ConfigMap-driven log retention and namespace scoping

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');
function signLog(logLine, secret) {
  return crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret)
    .update(logLine)
    .digest('hex');
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of live CNF config delivery under scale, using dynamic route management, traffic shaping, and robust rollback. It probes understanding of drift detection, observability integration, and safe rollout in multi-tenant environments.

## Key Concepts
- Zero-downtime rolling updates with canary deployments
- Dynamic configuration distribution and consistency
- Drift detection and automated rollback with observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation snippet to illustrate traffic weight update
async function rollWithCanary(nextWeight) {
  await distributeConfig({ tenants: 'all', weight: nextWeight });
  await monitorErrors(60_000);
  if (riskTooHigh()) rollback();
}
```

